# JWT Authentication API

A JWT-based authentication REST API built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB. Implements access/refresh token rotation, HTTP-only cookies, and role-based access control (RBAC).

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Runtime | Node.js (ESM — `"type": "module"`) |
| Framework | Express 5 |
| Database | MongoDB via Mongoose 9 |
| Auth | JSON Web Tokens (`jsonwebtoken`) |
| Password hashing | bcrypt |
| HTTP logging | Morgan |
| Cookie parsing | cookie-parser |
| Config | dotenv |

---

## Project Structure

```
auth/
├── server.js                              # Entry point — starts server & connects DB
└── src/
    ├── app.js                             # Express app, middleware, route mounting
    ├── config/
    │   ├── database.js                    # Mongoose connection
    │   └── temp.js                        # JWT_SECRET and config exports
    ├── controllers/
    │   ├── auth.controller.js             # register, login, getMe, refreshToken, changeRole
    │   └── dele.controller.js             # deleteUser (admin only)
    ├── middlewares/
    │   ├── authentication.middleware.js   # Verifies Bearer token, attaches req.user
    │   └── admin.middleware.js            # Checks req.user.role === 'admin'
    ├── models/
    │   └── user.model.js                  # User schema
    ├── routes/
    │   ├── auth.routes.js                 # /api/auth/* routes
    │   └── dele.route.js                  # /api/dele/* routes
    └── utils/
        └── generateTokens.js              # Signs and returns access + refresh tokens
```

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```env
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_here
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/auth
```

---

## Getting Started

```bash
npm install
npm run dev     # starts with nodemon on port 3000
```

Server runs at `http://localhost:3000`.

---

## API Endpoints

### Auth routes — `/api/auth`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth required | Role | Description |
|--------|----------|---------------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | No | — | Create a new user account |
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | No | — | Login, receive access token + refresh cookie |
| GET | `/api/auth/get-me` | Yes | any | Get the currently logged-in user's info |
| POST | `/api/auth/refresh-token` | No (cookie) | — | Issue new access + refresh tokens |
| PATCH | `/api/auth/update-role` | Yes | admin | Change another user's role |

### Delete routes — `/api/dele`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth required | Role | Description |
|--------|----------|---------------|------|-------------|
| DELETE | `/api/dele/users/:id` | Yes | admin | Delete a user by MongoDB `_id` |

---

## User Model

```js
{
    username:     { type: String,  required: true },
    email:        { type: String,  required: true, unique: true },
    password:     { type: String,  required: true },   // bcrypt hash
    refreshToken: { type: String },                    // stored for reuse detection
    role:         { type: String,  enum: ['user', 'admin', 'manager'],  default: 'user' }
}
```

---

## How It Works

### Register

- Validates all fields are present (`username`, `email`, `password`).
- Checks for duplicate email or username.
- Hashes password with bcrypt (10 salt rounds).
- Creates user with `role: 'user'` by default.
- Returns a success message — no tokens are issued at registration.

### Login

- Looks up user by email.
- Compares submitted password against the stored bcrypt hash.
- Generates a 15-minute access token and a 7-day refresh token.
- Saves the refresh token to the database.
- Sets the refresh token in an `httpOnly` cookie.
- Returns the access token and role in the response body.

### Get Me

- Reads the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.
- Verifies the token and fetches the user from the database (password and refreshToken excluded).
- Returns `username`, `email`, and `role`.

### Refresh Token

1. Reads the refresh token from the `httpOnly` cookie.
2. Verifies token signature and expiry.
3. Finds the user in the database.
4. Compares the incoming token against the stored token — mismatch means a stolen or replayed token, returning `401`.
5. Generates new access + refresh tokens (rotation).
6. Saves the new refresh token to the database, invalidating the old one.
7. Sets the new cookie and returns the new access token.

### Change Role (admin only)

- Requires `authenticate` + `admin` middleware.
- Accepts `userId` and `role` in the request body.
- Validates role is one of `user | manager | admin`.
- Updates the target user's role.

### Delete User (admin only)

- Requires `authenticate` + `admin` middleware.
- Deletes the target user by `req.params.id`.
- Prevents an admin from deleting their own account.

---

## Token Strategy

| Token | Lifetime | Transported via |
|-------|----------|-----------------|
| Access token | 15 minutes | Response body → `Authorization: Bearer` header |
| Refresh token | 7 days | `httpOnly` cookie only |

The short access-token lifetime limits the damage window if a token is leaked. The refresh token is never accessible to JavaScript, blocking XSS-based theft.

### Token rotation

Every successful call to `/refresh-token` issues brand-new tokens and invalidates the old refresh token in the database:

```
POST /login
  └── refresh token A saved to DB, set in cookie

POST /refresh-token  (cookie carries token A)
  ├── token A verified against DB  ✓
  ├── token B generated and saved to DB
  ├── token A is now invalid
  └── client receives token B in new cookie
```

---

## Cookie Security Flags

```js
res.cookie('refreshToken', refreshToken, {
    httpOnly: true,      // inaccessible to JavaScript — blocks XSS
    secure: true,        // HTTPS only
    sameSite: 'strict',  // no cross-origin requests — blocks CSRF
    maxAge: 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000   // 7 days in ms
});
```

---

## Middleware

### `authenticate`

Reads the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, verifies the JWT, fetches the matching user from the database (omitting `password` and `refreshToken`), and attaches the user to `req.user` before calling `next()`.

### `admin`

Checks `req.user.role === 'admin'`. Returns `403 Forbidden` if not. Must be placed after `authenticate` in the middleware chain.

---

## Role-Based Access Control

| Role | Permissions |
|------|------------|
| `user` | Access protected routes |
| `manager` | Same as `user` (extendable) |
| `admin` | Everything + change roles + delete users |

> The first admin must be set manually in MongoDB, since all users register as `user` by default. After that, the admin can promote others via `PATCH /api/auth/update-role`.

---

## Security Summary

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|-----------|
| XSS | Refresh token in `httpOnly` cookie — JS cannot read it |
| CSRF | `sameSite: strict` cookie flag |
| Token theft | Access token expires in 15 minutes |
| Stolen refresh token | Reuse detection — DB mismatch returns `401` |
| Brute force | bcrypt hashing slows password attacks |
| Privilege escalation | Role validated server-side on every admin action |
| Self-deletion | Admin cannot delete their own account |

---

## Testing with Postman

### Register

```
POST /api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "securepassword"
}

→ 201: { "message": "User registered successfully" }
```

### Login

```
POST /api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "securepassword"
}

→ 200: { "message": "Login successful", "token": "<accessToken>", "role": "user" }
→ Cookie set: refreshToken (httpOnly)
```

### Get Me

```
GET /api/auth/get-me
Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>

→ 200: { "message": "User fetched successfully", "user": { "username": "...", "email": "...", "role": "..." } }
```

### Refresh Token

```
POST /api/auth/refresh-token
(refreshToken cookie sent automatically)

→ 200: { "message": "Token refreshed successfully", "token": "<newAccessToken>" }
```

### Change Role (admin only)

```
PATCH /api/auth/update-role
Authorization: Bearer <adminAccessToken>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "userId": "<target MongoDB _id>",
    "role": "manager"
}

→ 200: { "message": "Role updated successfully" }
```

### Delete User (admin only)

```
DELETE /api/dele/users/<userId>
Authorization: Bearer <adminAccessToken>

→ 200: { "message": "User deleted successfully" }
```

---

## Full Auth Flow

```
POST /register
    └── account created, role: 'user', no tokens issued

POST /login
    ├── access token  → response body (15 min)
    └── refresh token → httpOnly cookie (7 days)

GET /get-me
    └── Authorization: Bearer <accessToken> → returns user data

Access token expires
    └── POST /refresh-token
            ├── cookie verified against DB
            ├── new access + refresh tokens issued
            └── repeats until refresh token expires (7 days)

Refresh token expires
    └── must POST /login again
```